---
description: Use CLI text tools only for known plain text files. Default to Python tooling for logs and structured data.
alwaysApply: true
---

### Use CLI text tools only for .txt files

- Restrict plain text utilities (grep, sed, awk, cut, tr, sort, uniq, head, tail, wc, strings, cat, less) to files with the .txt extension only.
- Do not apply these tools to mitmproxy .log files, JSON, or any other non-plain-text formats.

### Required handling for non-text data

- Mitmproxy .log files are binary. Use the project tools in ./tools/ or Python scripts to convert or query them.
- JSON and other structured data must be handled with Python scripts or dedicated tooling. Prefer Python modules (json, csv, pathlib) and project utilities in ./tools/.
- If uncertain about a file type, default to Python tooling rather than text utilities.

### Examples

- Allowed: grep "pattern" notes.txt
- Not allowed: grep "pattern" capture.log
- Preferred: python ./tools/log_to_json.py capture.log > capture.json, then process via Python
